 Exclusive Economic Zone","8376","mrgid","introduced",""],["Greece - Aegean Sea and Eastern Mediterranean","64209","mrgid","introduced",""],["Mozambican Coast","50303","mrgid","native",""],["Natal","21805","mrgid","native",""],["Turkish part of the Mediterranean Sea - Eastern Basin","25191","mrgid","introduced",""]]},"KCM2":{"v":[["Variable Anemone Eater","eng",0],["チャカミノモドキ","jpn",0]],"d":[["Mozambican Coast","50303","mrgid","native",""]]},"L2NJW":{"v":[["Boarmie tyrrhénienne (La)","fra",0],["Boarmie tyrrhénienne","fra",0]]},"MBVFB":{"v":[["Bahama Caracara","eng",0],["Bahaman Caracara","eng",0]],"d":[["Distribution. — Cave, asphalt and sinkhole deposits in west and central Cuba (see Appendix). Artemisa. Caimito: ACP (Suárez & Olson 2003 c: 305), ASA (Suárez & Arredondo 1997: 101, Suárez 2000 b: table 1 [‘ Caracara sp. ’], Suárez & Olson 2003 c: 305). Mayabeque. Quivicán: YTU (Suárez & Olson 2003 c: 307 [‘ Caracara plancus ssp. ’ of Jiménez Vázquez 1997 a: 49]). Matanzas. Cárdenas: MCA (Suárez & Arredondo 1997: 101, Suárez & Olson 2001 b: 502), Martí: MLB (Iturralde-Vinent et al. 2000: table 2 [‘ Caracara sp. ’], Suárez & Olson 2003 c: 307, Suárez 2020 a: 32). Jagüey Grande: MFJ (cf. CLV). Villa Clara. Corralillo: VSM (Suárez & Olson 2001 b: 502, Arredondo Antúnez & Villavicencio Finalet 2006: tables I – II). Direct 14 C dating. — None from Cuba. Bahamas, Late Holocene (Sawmill Sink): 2,650 to 2,350 Cal BP (Steadman & Franklin 2015: table 2, femur). Notes. — Common in Quaternary deposits in Cuba, from where the species seems to have originated and subsequently colonised the Lucayan Archipelago. Recorded from Cuba by Suárez & Arredondo (1997: 101), with additional material subsequently reported and the species redescribed (Suárez & Olson 2001 b, 2003 c, Suárez 2020 a). One record from Dolphin Cave on Grand Cayman, Cayman Islands (Morgan 1994: 480 [‘ Polyborus creightoni ’]) is considered erroneous (Suárez & Olson 2001 b: 507, Olson 2008: 265). The main features of Creighton’s Caracara vs. congenerics is the presence of a massive and differently shaped rostrum (Suárez & Olson 2001 b: 502, 2014: 308, Suárez 2020 a: 33). Orihuela (2019: 61) commented that ‘ Suárez & Olson (2001 a) hypothesised a recent arrival to Cuba [of C. creightoni], along with Cathartes. ’ but this is a misinterpretation (see Suárez 2020 a: 35). Figueredo (2011: 11) cited the species as ‘ ave de rapiña sin vuelo’ [‘ flightless bird of prey’], which is incorrect. For material and distribution of C. creightoni in the Bahamas, see Brodkorb (1959), Olson (1976), Olson & Hilgartner (1982), Steadman et al. (2007) and Steadman & Franklin (2015, 2020).","","text","",""]]},"P7895":{"v":[["lundhvitkjuke","nob",0],["Brunlig hovporesvamp","dan",0],["Brunlig sejporesvamp","dan",0]],"d":[["Denmark","DK","iso","","least concern"]]},"PQBTV":{"v":[["Peixe-anual","por",0]],"d":[["Global","","text","native","endangered"]]},"PW5Q":{"v":[["Sweetbay Silkmoth","eng",0],["木蘭蠶蛾","zho",0]]},"QMT9B":{"v":[["Vietnam Rice Frog","eng",0],["parosnička annamská","ces",0]]},"R6QT":{"v":[["Cardo agglomerato","ita",0],["Chardon aggloméré","fra",0],["Чертополох цветоголовчатый","rus",0]],"d":[["Corsica; Sardinia; Italy; Sicily; Algeria","","text","",""]]},"S7LW":{"v":[["Fiordaliso di Tommasini","ita",0]],"d":[["NE-Italy; Croatia","","text","",""]]},"WN35":{"v":[["lesser star-turris","eng",0]],"d":[["Caribbean Sea","4287","mrgid","",""],["Colombian part of the Caribbean Sea","25303","mrgid","",""],["Cuban Exclusive Economic Zone","8406","mrgid","",""],["Gulf of Mexico","4288","mrgid","",""],["Jamaican Exclusive Economic Zone","8459","mrgid","",""],["Lesser Antilles","19267","mrgid","",""],["Puerto Rican Exclusive Economic Zone","33179","mrgid","",""]]},"XK64":{"v":[["a-ou-méiou","por",0],["aimeyu","por",0],["arraieira-branca","por",0],["nuhba-jibamuhe","por",0],["palo-de-matajuare","por",0],["palo-de-matawar","por",0],["sacha zapote","spa",0],["Palo Tábano","spa",0]],"d":[["Colombia (Amazonas, C